# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets supports this file (same syntax as Cloudflare Pages)
# to set response headers per path. Without this, HTML pages were being cached
# aggressively enough that updates required an incognito window or manual cache
# clear to see — this forces every page load to revalidate with the origin first.
#
# "no-cache" does NOT mean "never cache" — it means the browser must revalidate
# (a fast conditional request) before using any cached copy, so repeat visits
# stay quick but never show stale content after a deploy.

/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/*.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
